    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup as our primary force; his score of 81.88 is bolstered by a favorable matchup against Ober and a high-leverage leadoff spot, making him an essential start. **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.40) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.45) also provide high-end production, with **Luis Robert Jr.** benefiting from a solid platoon edge against the lefty P\u00e9rez and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** thriving in his typical middle-of-the-order role. We are particularly aggressive with our stolen base targets today, leaning on the aggressive baserunning profiles of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Heliot Ramos** against pitchers with slower deliveries, despite the 31% rain risk clouding the matchups for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos** in the later innings.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished with a 46.31 score, narrowly missing the cut behind the superior daily efficiency of **Drake Baldwin** and **Sam Antonacci**. While **Nasim Nunez** offers intrigue for his speed upside, the unfavorable matchup against Imanaga combined with a bottom-of-the-order assignment suppressed his ceiling enough to keep him sidelined. We are also monitoring the lineup status for **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Liam Hicks** closely; should any of these presumed starters shift down in the order or be rested, we will need to re-evaluate the utility of our bench depth. With **Jordan Westburg** currently on the IL, our roster flexibility is limited, placing a premium on the performance of starters like **Coby Mayo** and **Miguel Vargas**, who both carry enough SP-skill leverage today to justify their inclusion despite varying platoon dynamics.",
